.TH SCS-DBMIGRATE 1 "September 2026" "sslcrtsrv 0.8.4" "SSLCrtSrv Manual"
.SH NAME
scs-dbmigrate \- SSLCrtSrv database schema upgrades and cross-backend data migration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs-dbmigrate
.RI [ \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR ]
.RI { upgrade-schema " | " migrate }
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs-dbmigrate
is deliberately the only tool in this project that touches schema DDL or
copies data between database backends; every other tool only ever creates a
fresh, up-to-date, empty schema on first run.
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
Default
.IR /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B upgrade-schema
Bring the currently configured backend's schema up to date in place. Safe to
run repeatedly \(em a no-op once already current, and a no-op against a
brand-new database. Run this once after upgrading
.B sslcrtsrv
past a version that changed the schema, before starting any other tool.
.TP
.BI "migrate " "\-\-to\-backend {sqlite,mysql,postgresql} [options]"
Copy every client/certificate/permission row to a freshly created target
backend, then repoint
.IR server_config.json " at it. Leaves the source backend/data untouched."
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-to\-backend " "{sqlite,mysql,postgresql}"
Required. Target database backend.
.TP
.BI "\-\-host " HOST ", \-\-port " PORT ", \-\-user " USER ", \-\-password " PASSWORD ", \-\-database " NAME
Target connection details. Prompted for interactively if not given as a
flag and needed for the chosen backend.
.RE
.PP
A
.I client_certificate_relations
row referencing a client or certificate no longer present in the source is
skipped and printed, not treated as fatal. A missing database driver
(PyMySQL/psycopg2) or an unreachable target reports a plain, actionable error
instead of a raw traceback.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json
\(em default configuration file; updated in place by
.B migrate
once the copy succeeds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scs-server (1)
.PP
The project's
.I Manual.MD
has the full narrative reference, including a fresh MySQL/PostgreSQL setup
walkthrough.
.SH AUTHOR
Garry Glendown
